  "metaDescription": "Former National Police Chief Listyo Sigit Prabowo did not attend an ethics hearing regarding wiretapping allegations, causing a delay until next week.",
  "aiSummaryBullets": [
    "Former National Police Chief Listyo Sigit Prabowo declined to attend a professional ethics hearing concerning wiretapping allegations.",
    "The disciplinary committee postponed the proceeding until Monday of the following week due to his absence.",
    "Police officials stated that no special treatment is provided and that failing to appear may lead to the forfeiture of defense and appeal rights."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "Former Indonesian National Police Chief Listyo Sigit Prabowo has declined to appear at a scheduled professional ethics hearing related to alleged unauthorized wiretapping involving the President. The National Police stated that the proceedings have been rescheduled for next Monday. Authorities have clarified that there is no special treatment for individuals who fail to attend these sessions, noting that the regulations governing the Police Code of Ethics Commission are applied consistently. Representatives from the National Police Commission (Kompolnas) indicated that missing such hearings is a procedural issue that has historical precedents within the force. Observers note that if the individual continues to remain absent at the rescheduled date, they risk losing critical legal rights, including the opportunity to present a formal defense and the right to file an appeal against potential disciplinary findings.",
